{
  "description": "Payloads that must and must not start an orchestrate hand-off, and payloads the agent.yml Gate must park for the workflow-path route. CI jq evaluates fire() and parks() against each case; needles must appear in the named workflow so the if: and the Gate jq cannot drift from this file. cap_cases run the orchestrate job's real 'Check the issue is still parked' script against a fake gh serving each case's issue comments (handoffs are today's 'orchestrator hand-off started:' comments from a member, overridable by when YESTERDAY, assoc and body; noise adds that many unrelated comments; fail_comments 5xx's the list that many times; fail_post fails the marker post); a go=true case must post the marker; CI asserts go, model and turns, so removing the cap, the model pin or the turns pin fails it. session_cases run the real session step against a fake claude and assert its argv, so removing --settings disableAllHooks fails it. Every claude session case also asserts the start-up trim flags --strict-mcp-config, --disable-slash-commands and --setting-sources project,local (the pi cases are exempt), so deleting one fails CI. Runner (fleet-ops#9407): cap_cases assert want_runner (pi or claude) from the issue step; session_cases with runner pi run the real step against a fake pi and assert provider litellm, the seat, and FLEET_TASK_ID.",
  "needles": {
    "agent-dispatch.yml": [
      "ORCHESTRATE",
      "needs-orchestrator",
      "orchestrate",
      "nish3451",
      "nishfleet-worker[bot]",
      "github-actions[bot]",
      "handoff-ended",
      "orch/issue-",
      "--max-turns \"$TURNS\"",
      "ORCHESTRATE_DAILY_MAX",
      "claude-sonnet-5-5",
      "ORCHESTRATE_HOOKS",
      "actions: read",
      "disableAllHooks",
      "--output-format json",
      "--permission-mode bypassPermissions",
      "--strict-mcp-config",
      "--disable-slash-commands",
      "--setting-sources project,local",
      "cancel-in-progress: false",
      "vars.ORCHESTRATE != 'off' && (",
      "github.event.label.name == 'needs-orchestrator'",
      "github.event.sender.login == 'nish3451'",
      "inputs.task == 'orchestrate' && inputs.issue != ''",
      "ORCHESTRATE_RUNNER",
      "ORCHESTRATE_SEAT",
      "--provider litellm",
      "orchestrator hand-off started:"
    ],
    "agent.yml": [
      ".github/workflows/",
      "needs-orchestrator",
      "agent-ready,agent-in-progress",
      "workflow-files",
      "routed: the deliverable edits .github/workflows/**, which the worker App cannot push; handed to the orchestrator",
      "fleet_ops=false"
    ]
  },
